behavior guard: The top_n function should return a list of length n containing elements from the input list. (passes on the current code)
Change top_n to return the n largest values by sorting in descending order.
--- a/inventory.py
+++ b/inventory.py
@@ -17,3 +17,3 @@
 def top_n(values, n):
     """Return the n largest values, largest first."""
-    return sorted(values)[:n]
+    return sorted(values, reverse=True)[:n]
